      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u make me a 4 week lifting program? im 35, work an office job, and i want to start doing more compound lifts like squats and deadlifts. just looking for a basic linear progression thing to get started since im a beginner. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can provide you with a basic 4-week lifting program focused on compound exercises. \n\n**Weeks 1-2:**\n\n- Monday: Squats (3 sets of 8 reps)\n- Tuesday: Deadlifts (3 sets of 8 reps)\n- Thursday: Bench Press (3 sets of 8 reps)\n- Friday: Pull-ups (or Assisted Pull-ups) (3 sets of as many reps as possible)\n- Sunday: Walk or light Cardio\n\n**Weeks 3-4:**\n\n- Increase Squats by 2.5-5lbs (depending on your progress)\n- Increase Deadlifts by 2.5-5lbs (depending on your progress)\n- Maintain or decrease Bench Press as needed\n- Increase Pull-ups by one rep per set\n- Sunday remains the same\n\nPlease consult a doctor or a certified personal trainer before starting any new exercise program. As someone with an office job, make sure you warm up properly before each workout, and prioritize proper form over heavy weights.",
